# 2. DFS Returning Height

## Question Asked to Every Node

```text
What is the height of your subtree?
```

## Meaning of Recursive Results

```text
left  = Height of the left subtree
right = Height of the right subtree
```

## Formula

```text
Current height = 1 + maximum left or right height
```

## Code

```java
private int dfs(TreeNode root) {

    // An empty tree has a height of 0.
    if (root == null) {
        return 0;
    }

    // Get the height of the left subtree.
    int leftHeight = dfs(root.left);

    // Get the height of the right subtree.
    int rightHeight = dfs(root.right);

    // Include the current node and choose the taller side.
    return 1 + Math.max(leftHeight, rightHeight);
}
```

## Used In

- Maximum Depth of Binary Tree
- Height of a Binary Tree
- Diameter of Binary Tree
- Balanced Binary Tree

