# 3. DFS Returning Node Count

## Question Asked to Every Node

```text
How many nodes are present in your subtree?
```

## Meaning of Recursive Results

```text
left  = Number of nodes in the left subtree
right = Number of nodes in the right subtree
```

## Formula

```text
Current subtree count = 1 + left count + right count
```

## Code

```java
private int dfs(TreeNode root) {

    // An empty tree contains 0 nodes.
    if (root == null) {
        return 0;
    }

    // Count the nodes in the left subtree.
    int leftCount = dfs(root.left);

    // Count the nodes in the right subtree.
    int rightCount = dfs(root.right);

    // Add left nodes, right nodes, and the current node.
    return 1 + leftCount + rightCount;
}
```

## Used In

- Count Nodes in a Binary Tree
- Tree Size
- Count Complete Tree Nodes

