# 4. DFS Returning Subtree Sum

## Question Asked to Every Node

```text
What is the sum of all node values in your subtree?
```

## Meaning of Recursive Results

```text
left  = Sum of the left subtree
right = Sum of the right subtree
```

## Formula

```text
Current subtree sum = current value + left sum + right sum
```

## Code

```java
private int dfs(TreeNode root) {

    // An empty tree contributes 0 to the sum.
    if (root == null) {
        return 0;
    }

    // Calculate the sum of the left subtree.
    int leftSum = dfs(root.left);

    // Calculate the sum of the right subtree.
    int rightSum = dfs(root.right);

    // Add the current node value to both subtree sums.
    return root.val + leftSum + rightSum;
}
```

## Used In

- Binary Tree Sum
- Subtree Sum
- Most Frequent Subtree Sum

