# 5. DFS Returning Boolean

## Question Asked to Every Node

```text
Does your subtree satisfy the required condition?
```

## Meaning of Recursive Results

```text
left  = Does the left subtree satisfy the condition?
right = Does the right subtree satisfy the condition?
```

## General Code

```java
private boolean dfs(TreeNode root) {

    // An empty subtree is normally considered valid.
    if (root == null) {
        return true;
    }

    // Check the left subtree.
    boolean leftValid = dfs(root.left);

    // Check the right subtree.
    boolean rightValid = dfs(root.right);

    // The current subtree is valid only when both sides are valid.
    return leftValid && rightValid;
}
```

## Important Note

The exact condition differs between problems. For example:

```text
Same Tree      -> Compare both nodes and their subtrees.
Symmetric Tree -> Compare the left side with the mirrored right side.
Validate BST   -> Check whether values are inside an allowed range.
Path Sum       -> Check whether a root-to-leaf path reaches the target.
```

