# 6. Return Height and Update a Global Answer

This is the pattern used in **Diameter of Binary Tree**.

The recursive function and the global variable have two different jobs:

```text
dfs() returns height to the parent.

diameter stores the best diameter found anywhere in the tree.
```

## Why Two Values Are Needed

The parent needs the child's height so that the parent can continue building a path upward.

However, the complete diameter might pass through any node in the tree. Therefore, every node checks whether it creates a better diameter and updates the global answer.

## Complete Code

